#: ../../../dev/events.rst:4
msgid "Event API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:7
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:9
msgid ""
"Syncthing provides a simple long polling interface for exposing events from "
"the core utility towards a GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:12
msgid ""
"To receive events, perform a HTTP GET of ``/rest/events?"
"since=<lastSeenID>``, where ``<lastSeenID>`` is the ID of the last event "
"you've already seen or zero. Syncthing returns a JSON encoded array of event "
"objects, starting at the event just after the one with the last seen ID. "
"There is a limit to the number of events buffered, so if the rate of events "
"is high or the time between polling calls is long some events might be "
"missed. This can be detected by noting a discontinuity in the event IDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:20
msgid ""
"If no new events are produced since ``<lastSeenID>``, the HTTP call blocks "
"and waits for new events to happen before returning, or if no new events are "
"produced within 60 seconds, times out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:24
msgid ""
"To receive only a limited number of events, add the ``limit=n`` parameter "
"with a suitable value for ``n`` and only the *last* ``n`` events will be "
"returned. This can be used to catch up with the latest event ID after a "
"disconnection for example: ``/rest/events?since=0&limit=1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:30
msgid "Event Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:32
msgid "Each event is represented by an object similar to the following::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:34
msgid ""
"{\n"
"    \"id\": 2,\n"
"    \"type\": \"DeviceConnected\",\n"
"    \"time\": \"2014-07-13T21:04:33.687836696+02:00\",\n"
"    \"data\": {\n"
"        \"addr\": \"172.16.32.25:22000\",\n"
"        \"id\": \"NFGKEKE-7Z6RTH7-I3PRZXS-DEJF3UJ-FRWJBFO-VBBTDND-4SGNGVZ-"
"QUQHJAG\"\n"
"    }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:44
msgid ""
"The top level keys ``id``, ``time``, ``type`` and ``data`` are always "
"present, though ``data`` may be ``null``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:47
msgid "id"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:48
msgid ""
"A monotonically increasing integer. The first event generated has id ``1``, "
"the next has id ``2`` etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:50
msgid "time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:51
msgid "The time the event was generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:52
msgid "type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:53
msgid ""
"Indicates the type of (i.e. reason for) the event and is one of the event "
"types below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:55
msgid "data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/events.rst:56
msgid ""
"An object containing optional extra information; the exact structure is "
"determined by the event type."
msgstr ""

